Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||09-27-2000||01:20 PM||||i have a 1987 gt (v-6, 5spd.) and am pretty darn sure my engine or tranny (or both?) mounts are going south. i already know i need to replace the dog bone bushings (there is an imprint of a nut in the metal- the dog bone whacked around and hit something) and was looking into changing all the other moutnts at the same time. i went to napa autoparts and the guy said that he only showed one engine mount - is that right? also, what are the dogbone bushings called? thanks, and sorry about the long winded way i have of saying things<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1012904&a=7460599&p=25516673"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FST2M6||09-27-2000||01:31 PM||||yeah hes right.. one engine mount at the passengerside oil pan and 2 tranny mounts.. PLUS a lame vibration "torsional dampener" pseudo strut thing.. and the dog bone. thats it... take about 3 hours to change them all in your garage with a floor jack and PB BLaster.. ||||reg||1
